ills/gws-sheets-read resolved=~/gws-cli/skills/gws-sheets-read\n[skills] Skipping escaped skill path outside its configured root: source=openclaw-managed root=~/.openclaw/skills reason=symlink-escape requested=~/.openclaw/skills/gws-slides resolved=~/gws-cli/skills/gws-slides\n[skills] Skipping escaped skill path outside its configured root: source=openclaw-managed root=~/.openclaw/skills reason=symlink-escape requested=~/.openclaw/skills/gws-tasks resolved=~/gws-cli/skills/gws-tasks\n[skills] Skipping escaped skill path outside its configured root: source=openclaw-managed root=~/.openclaw/skills reason=symlink-escape requested=~/.openclaw/skills/gws-workflow resolved=~/gws-cli/skills/gws-workflow\n[skills] Skipping escaped skill path outside its configured root: source=openclaw-managed root=~/.openclaw/skills reason=symlink-escape requested=~/.openclaw/skills/gws-workflow-email-to-task resolved=~/gws-cli/skills/gws-workflow-email-to-task\n[skills] Skipping escaped skill path outside its configured root: source=openclaw-managed root=~/.openclaw/skills reason=symlink-escape requested=~/.openclaw/skills/gws-workflow-file-announce resolved=~/gws-cli/skills/gws-workflow-file-announce\n[skills] Skipping escaped skill path outside its configured root: source=openclaw-managed root=~/.openclaw/skills reason=symlink-escape requested=~/.openclaw/skills/gws-workflow-meeting-prep resolved=~/gws-cli/skills/gws-workflow-meeting-prep\n[skills] Skipping escaped skill path outside its configured root: source=openclaw-managed root=~/.openclaw/skills reason=symlink-escape requested=~/.openclaw/skills/gws-workflow-standup-report resolved=~/gws-cli/skills/gws-workflow-standup-report\n[skills] Skipping escaped skill path outside its configured root: source=openclaw-managed root=~/.openclaw/skills reason=symlink-escape requested=~/.openclaw/skills/gws-workflow-weekly-digest resolved=~/gws-cli/skills/gws-workflow-weekly-digest\n[skills] Skipping escaped skill path outside its configured root: source=agents-skills-personal root=~/.agents/skills reason=symlink-escape requested=~/.agents/skills/weather/SKILL.md resolved=~/.openclaw/workspace/skills/weather/SKILL.md\nOpenClaw security audit\nSummary: 6 critical · 5 warn · 1 info\nRun deeper: openclaw security audit --deep\n\nCRITICAL\nsecurity.exposure.open_groups_with_elevated Open groupPolicy with elevated tools enabled\n  Found groupPolicy=\"open\" at:\n- channels.telegram.groupPolicy\nWith tools.elevated enabled, a prompt injection in those rooms can become a high-impact incident.\n  Fix: Set groupPolicy=\"allowlist\" and keep elevated allowlists extremely tight.\nsecurity.exposure.open_groups_with_runtime_or_fs Open groupPolicy with runtime/filesystem tools exposed\n  Found groupPolicy=\"open\" at:\n- channels.telegram.groupPolicy\nRisky tool exposure contexts:\n- agents.defaults (sandbox=off; runtime=[exec, process]; fs=[read, write, edit, apply_patch]; fs.workspaceOnly=false)\n- agents.list.main (sandbox=off; runtime=[exec, process]; fs=[read, write, edit, apply_patch]; fs.workspaceOnly=false)\nPrompt injection in open groups can trigger command/file actions in these contexts.\n  Fix: For open groups, prefer tools.profile=\"messaging\" (or deny group:runtime/group:fs), set tools.fs.workspaceOnly=true, and use agents.defaults.sandbox.mode=\"all\" for exposed agents.\nplugins.code_safety Plugin \"claude-mem\" contains dangerous code patterns\n  Found 6 critical issue(s) in 10 scanned file(s):\n  - [dangerous-exec] Shell command execution detected (child_process) (plugin/scripts/bun-runner.js:51)\n  - [dangerous-exec] Shell command execution detected (child_process) (plugin/scripts/mcp-server.cjs:6)\n  - [dynamic-code-execution] Dynamic code execution detected (plugin/scripts/mcp-server.cjs:6)\n  - [env-harvesting] Environment variable access combined with network send — possible credential harvesting (plugin/scripts/mcp-server.cjs:57)\n  - [dangerous-exec] Shell command execution detected (child_process) (plugin/scripts/smart-install.js:78)\n  - [env-harvesting] Environment variable access combined with network send — possible credential harvesting (plugin/scripts/worker-cli.js:5)\n  Fix: Review the plugin source code carefully before use. If untrusted, remove the plugin from your OpenClaw extensions state directory.\nskills.code_safety Skill \"tavily\" contains dangerous code patterns\n  Found 2 critical issue(s) in 2 scanned file(s) under /home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/skills/tavily-search:\n  - [env-harvesting] Environment variable access combined with network send — possible credential harvesting (scripts/extract.mjs:25)\n  - [env-harvesting] Environment variable access combined with network send — possible credential harvesting (scripts/search.mjs:49)\n  Fix: Review the skill source code before use. If untrusted, remove \"/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/skills/tavily-search\".\nskills.code_safety Skill \"writing-skills\" contains dangerous code patterns\n  Found 1 critical issue(s) in 1 scanned file(s) under /home/lfant/.agents/skills/writing-skills:\n  - [dangerous-exec] Shell command execution detected (child_process) (render-graphs.js:25)\n  Fix: Review the skill source code before use. If untrusted, remove \"/home/lfant/.agents/skills/writing-skills\".\nchannels.telegram.warning.1 Telegram security warning\n  Telegram groups: groupPolicy=\"open\" with no channels.telegram.groups allowlist; any group can add + ping (mention-gated). Set channels.telegram.groupPolicy=\"allowlist\" + channels.telegram.groupAllowFrom or configure channels.telegram.groups.\n\nWARN\ngateway.trusted_proxies_missing Reverse proxy headers are not trusted\n  gateway.bind is loopback and gateway.trustedProxies is empty. If you expose the Control UI through a reverse proxy, configure trusted proxies so local-client checks cannot be spoofed.\n  Fix: Set gateway.trustedProxies to your proxy IPs or keep the Control UI local-only.\ntools.exec.auto_allow_skills_enabled autoAllowSkills is enabled for exec approvals\n  Implicit skill-bin allowlisting is enabled at:\n- defaults.autoAllowSkills\nThis widens host exec trust beyond explicit manual allowlist entries.\n  Fix: Disable autoAllowSkills in exec approvals and keep manual allowlists tight when you need explicit host-exec trust.\nsecurity.trust_model.multi_user_heuristic Potential multi-user setup detected (personal-assistant model warning)\n  Heuristic signals indicate this gateway may be reachable by multiple users:\n- channels.telegram.groupPolicy=\"open\"\nRuntime/process tools are exposed without full sandboxing in at least one context.\nPotential high-impact tool exposure contexts:\n- agents.defaults (sandbox=off; runtime=[exec, process]; fs=[read, write, edit, apply_patch]; fs.workspaceOnly=false)\n- agents.list.main (sandbox=off; runtime=[exec, process]; fs=[read, write, edit, apply_patch]; fs.workspaceOnly=false)\nOpenClaw's default security model is personal-assistant (one trusted operator boundary), not hostile multi-tenant isolation on one shared gateway.\n  Fix: If users may be mutually untrusted, split trust boundaries (separate gateways + credentials, ideally separate OS users/hosts). If you intentionally run shared-user access, set agents.defaults.sandbox.mode=\"all\", keep tools.fs.workspaceOnly=true, deny runtime/fs/web tools unless required, and keep personal/private identities + credentials off that runtime.\nplugins.allow_phantom_entries plugins.allow contains entries with no matching installed plugin\n  The following plugins.allow entries do not correspond to any installed plugin: telegram, memory-core, zai, openai, openrouter.\nPhantom entries could be exploited by registering a new plugin with an allowlisted ID.\n  Fix: Remove unused entries from plugins.allow, or verify the expected plugins are installed.\nplugins.tools_reachable_permissive_policy Extension plugin tools may be reachable under permissive tool policy\n  Enabled extension plugins: claude-mem.\nPermissive tool policy contexts:\n- default\n- agents.list.main\n  Fix: Use restrictive profiles (`minimal`/`coding`) or explicit tool allowlists that exclude plugin tools for agents handling untrusted input.\n\nINFO\nsummary.attack_surface Attack surface summary\n  groups: open=1, allowlist=0\ntools.elevated: enabled\nhooks.webhooks: disabled\nhooks.internal: enabled\nbrowser control: enabled\ntrust model: personal assistant (one trusted operator boundary), not hostile multi-tenant on one shared gateway\n[agents/auth-profiles] synced openai-codex credentials from external cli\n","name":"openclaw security"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1776794450500}}
{"type":"message","id":"c61bf2f2","parentId":"63c0264e","timestamp":"2026-04-21T18:01:59.143Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good, I have the security audit results. Now I need to filter out the false positives as instructed by the user:\n\n**False positives to ignore:**\n1. tavily-search: scripts/extract.mjs, scripts/search.mjs\n2. claude-mem: bun-runner.js, context-generator.cjs, mcp-server.cjs, smart-install.js, worker-cli.js\n3. writing-skills: render-graphs.js\n\nLet me review the critical findings:\n\n1. **security.exposure.open_groups_with_elevated** - Critical issue about open group policy with elevated tools\n   - This is NOT a false positive - it's a real security concern\n\n2. **security.exposure.open_groups_with_runtime_or_fs** - Critical issue about open group policy with runtime/filesystem tools\n   - This is NOT a false positive - it's a real security concern\n\n3. **plugins.code_safety Plugin \"claude-mem\"** - 6 critical issues in 10 files\n   - bun-runner.js:51 - dangerous-exec\n   - mcp-server.cjs:6 - dangerous-exec, dynamic-code-execution\n   - mcp-server.cjs:57 - env-harvesting\n   - smart-install.js:78 - dangerous-exec\n   - worker-cli.js:5 - env-harvesting\n   - This SHOULD be ignored as per the user's instruction\n\n4. **skills.code_safety Skill \"tavily\"** - 2 critical issues in tavily-search\n   - scripts/extract.mjs:25 - env-harvesting\n   - scripts/search.mjs:49 - env-harvesting\n   - This SHOULD be ignored as per the user's instruction\n\n5. **skills.code_safety Skill \"writing-skills\"** - 1 critical issue\n   - render-graphs.js:25 - dangerous-exec\n   - This SHOULD be ignored as per the user's instruction\n\nI'll filter out the tavily-search, claude-mem, and writing-skills findings, focusing on the two critical issues about open group policy and tool exposure.\n\nThe remaining critical alerts involve potential multi-user risks and a Telegram security warning. These highlight vulnerabilities in the current group policy configuration, which could potentially expose elevated tools to unintended users.\n\nI'll investigate the phantom entries and proxy settings, noting they aren't immediate critical concerns but warrant attention for overall system security.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"---\n\n## Security Audit Report\n\n**Run:** openclaw security audit --deep\n**Timestamp:** 2026-04-22 03:00 AM KST\n\n---\n\n### Summary (After Filtering False Positives)\n\n**4 CRITICAL · 5 WARN · 1 INFO**\n\n**Ignored False Positives:**\n- tavily-search (scripts/extract.mjs, scripts/search.mjs)\n- claude-mem (bun-runner.js, context-generator.cjs, mcp-server.cjs, smart-install.js, worker-cli.js)\n- writing-skills (render-graphs.js)\n\n---\n\n### Critical Issues\n\n#### 1. Open Groups with Elevated Tools Enabled\n**Risk:** Prompt injection in open groups can become a high-impact incident\n\n**Location:** channels.telegram.groupPolicy=\"open\"\n\n**Context:** With tools.elevated enabled, unauthorized users in Telegram groups could potentially execute elevated commands through prompt injection attacks.\n\n**Recommended Action:**\n- Set `groupPolicy=\"allowlist\"` in channels.telegram configuration\n- Restrict elevated tool access to only trusted/administrative groups\n- Maintain extremely tight allowlists for elevated operations\n\n---\n\n#### 2. Open Groups with Runtime/Filesystem Tools Exposed\n**Risk:** Prompt injection in open groups can trigger command/file actions\n\n**Location:** channels.telegram.groupPolicy=\"open\"\n\n**Exposed Contexts:**\n- agents.defaults (sandbox=off; runtime=[exec, process]; fs=[read, write, edit, apply_patch]; fs.workspaceOnly=false)\n- agents.list.main (sandbox=off; runtime=[exec, process]; fs=[read, write, edit, apply_patch]; fs.workspaceOnly=false)\n\n**Recommended Action:**\n- For open groups, prefer `tools.profile=\"messaging\"`\n- Deny group:runtime and group:fs tools\n- Set `tools.fs.workspaceOnly=true`\n- Use `agents.defaults.sandbox.mode=\"all\"` for exposed agents\n\n---\n\n#### 3. Multi-User Setup Warning\n**Risk:** Personal-assistant trust model may not be appropriate for multi-user access\n\n**Heuristic Signals:**\n- channels.telegram.groupPolicy=\"open\"\n\n**Exposed High-Impact Contexts:**\n- agents.defaults (sandbox=off; runtime=[exec, process]; fs=[read, write, edit, apply_patch]; fs.workspaceOnly=false)\n- agents.list.main (sandbox=off; runtime=[exec, process]; fs=[read, write, edit, apply_patch]; fs.workspaceOnly=false)\n\n**Recommended Action:**\n- If users may be mutually untrusted, split trust boundaries:\n  - Separate gateways + credentials\n  - Ideally separate OS users/hosts\n- If intentionally running shared-user access:\n  - Set `agents.defaults.sandbox.mode=\"all\"`\n  - Keep `tools.fs.workspaceOnly=true`\n  - Deny runtime/fs/web tools unless required\n  - Keep personal/private identities + credentials off that runtime\n\n---\n\n#### 4. Telegram Security Warning\n**Risk:** Any group can add and ping the agent with groupPolicy=\"open\"\n\n**Configuration:**\n- groupPolicy=\"open\"\n- No channels.telegram.groups allowlist configured\n\n**Recommended Action:**\n- Set `channels.telegram.groupPolicy=\"allowlist\"`\n- Configure `channels.telegram.groupAllowFrom` or\n- Configure `channels.telegram.groups` with specific trusted groups\n\n---\n\n### Warning Issues\n\n#### 1. Reverse Proxy Headers Not Trusted\n**Impact:** If Control UI is exposed through reverse proxy, local-client checks can be spoofed\n\n**Fix:** Set `gateway.trustedProxies` to proxy IPs or keep Control UI local-only\n\n#### 2. autoAllowSkills Enabled for Exec Approvals\n**Impact:** Widens host exec trust beyond explicit manual allowlist entries\n\n**Fix:** Disable `autoAllowSkills` in exec approvals and keep manual allowlists tight\n\n#### 3. Phantom Plugin Entries in plugins.allow\n**Issue:** The following entries do not correspond to any installed plugin:\n- telegram\n- memory-core\n- zai\n- openai\n- openrouter\n\n**Risk:** Could be exploited by registering a new plugin with an allowlisted ID\n\n**Fix:** Remove unused entries from plugins.allow or verify expected plugins are installed\n\n#### 4. Extension Plugin Tools Reachable Under Permissive Policy\n**Enabled Plugins:** claude-mem\n**Permissive Contexts:** default, agents.list.main\n\n**Fix:** Use restrictive profiles (`minimal`/`coding`) or explicit tool allowlists excluding plugin tools for agents handling untrusted input\n\n---\n\n### Info - Attack Surface Summary\n\n- **Groups:** open=1, allowlist=0\n- **Tools Elevated:** enabled\n- **Hooks Webhooks:** disabled\n- **Hooks Internal:** enabled\n- **Browser Control:** enabled\n- **Trust Model:** personal assistant (one trusted operator boundary)\n\n---\n\n### Priority Recommendations\n\n1. **Immediate:** Review Telegram group policy settings and implement allowlist\n2. **High:** Enable sandboxing for agents exposed to open groups\n3. **Medium:** Clean up phantom plugin entries in plugins.allow\n4. **Low:** Configure trusted proxies if reverse proxy is used\n\n---\n\n**Audit Complete.**"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"zai","model":"glm-4.7","usage":{"input":3927,"output":2039,"cacheRead":15347,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":21313,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1776794450506,"responseId":"2026042202005307d1688be017454b"}}
